{#
  review-ticket.j2 — ticket-aware review prompt (PASS/FAIL/DEFER + commit message).

  Evaluates the implementation against the originating Linear ticket.
  Reviewer also authors the commit message from what was actually built.

  Required state: ticket_title, ticket_description (written by fetch-ticket).
  Required inputs: linear_id.
  submit_tool_name injected by the contract engine.
#}
Review the implementation of Linear ticket {{ inputs.linear_id }} — **{{ state.ticket_title }}**.

## Acceptance criteria

{{ state.ticket_description }}

## Review criteria

Evaluate against: correctness relative to the acceptance criteria above, adequate test coverage, focused diff (no drive-by changes), no obvious regressions. Read the diff or relevant files, then identify issues.

Be concrete — point to file and line where possible. A clean review (no findings) is a valid result; do not invent issues to fill space.

## Verdict

Choose exactly one:

- **PASS** — nothing to report. The implementation is correct, tested, and focused.
  `issues` must be empty. If you would write anything into `issues`, you cannot choose
  PASS — choose FAIL or DEFER instead.
- **FAIL** — one or more findings that must be fixed before shipping. Use this for any
  finding the implementer could address in this session. Severity does not matter — a
  LOW finding that is fixable is still FAIL. Stale documentation, N+1 queries, missed
  spec updates: all FAIL.
- **DEFER** — a finding that is genuinely out of scope for this ticket: requires
  architectural redesign, a new spec, or work clearly beyond this ticket's boundary.
  The current code is shippable as-is; the deferred item becomes its own Linear ticket.
  Use DEFER sparingly — only when a fix cannot reasonably land in this session. If in
  doubt, use FAIL.

On FAIL: populate `issues` with each finding (file:line, description). Leave
`commit_message` empty and `deferred_brief` empty.

On PASS: `issues` is empty. Write `commit_message`.

On DEFER: populate `issues` with the deferred finding. Write `commit_message` (the
current code ships). Write `deferred_brief` as a one-line ticket title for the new
Linear issue.

## Commit message

Required for PASS and DEFER. Once you have read the diff, write a commit message
describing what was actually built — not the ticket title. Format:
`type(scope): description` where type is one of `feat / fix / chore / refactor / test`.
One line, under 72 characters.

When done, call {{ submit_tool_name | default('submit') }} exactly once with the verdict,
issues list, commit message, and deferred_brief.
